---
import { marked } from "marked";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site, getPage } from "../site";

const home = getPage("/") ?? site.pages[0];
const html = marked.parse(home.content) as string;
---
<Base title={home.title} description={site.site.description} pageSlug="/">
  <h1>{site.site.name}</h1>
  <p class="tagline">{site.site.tagline}</p>
  <article set:html={html} />

  <!-- ══ PROGRAMS SECTION ══ -->
  <section class="programs-section">
    <div class="programs-header">
      <h2 class="programs-heading">Six programs, one arc.</h2>
      <p class="programs-standfirst">A child can meet us in kindergarten and still be with us at nineteen — first as a reader, then as a mentee, then on our payroll.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 01 Flagship -->
    <div class="program-flagship">
      <span class="program-flagship-label">01 — Flagship</span>
      <a class="program-flagship-title" href="/read-2-succeed">Read 2 Succeed</a>
      <p class="program-flagship-body">One-to-one reading, phonics and vocabulary tutoring for children in kindergarten through second grade, delivered inside eight public and charter schools from January to June. Volunteers need no teaching background; training, materials, fingerprinting and background checks are provided.</p>
      <div class="program-tags">
        <span class="program-tag">Grades K–2</span>
        <span class="program-tag">1 hour weekly</span>
        <span class="program-tag">Jan–Jun</span>
        <span class="program-tag program-tag-dark">178 children, 2024–25</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Secondary grid -->
    <div class="programs-grid">
      <!-- 02 -->
      <div class="program-card">
        <span class="program-card-num">02</span>
        <h3 class="program-card-title">HopeKidz</h3>
        <p class="program-card-body">A Christian after-school club — literacy, games, a snack — running thirty weeks a year in five elementary schools. Three of the five serve NYCHA families.</p>
        <span class="program-card-meta">65 Children Weekly · Oct–Jun · K–5</span>
      </div>
      <!-- 03 -->
      <div class="program-card">
        <span class="program-card-num">03</span>
        <h3 class="program-card-title">Ambassadors of Peace</h3>
        <p class="program-card-body">A thirty-week mentorship for middle and high schoolers: college and career readiness, weekly small groups on stress and emotional health, and family outreach.</p>
        <span class="program-card-meta">30 Weeks · Grade 6 and Up</span>
      </div>
      <!-- 04 -->
      <div class="program-card">
        <span class="program-card-num">04</span>
        <h3 class="program-card-title">Summer Youth Employment</h3>
        <p class="program-card-body">We are an NYC SYEP employer for the third year running. Twenty-four young people worked twenty-five paid hours a week for six weeks; nine came from Park Hill.</p>
        <span class="program-card-meta">24 Teens · Paid · City Program</span>
      </div>
      <!-- 05 -->
      <div class="program-card">
        <span class="program-card-num">05</span>
        <h3 class="program-card-title">Summer Streets</h3>
        <p class="program-card-body">Five simultaneous day camps across the summer, on blocks the NYPD closes for us, in the neighborhoods where the reading gap widens fastest.</p>
        <span class="program-card-meta">5 Camps · Jul–Aug</span>
      </div>
      <!-- 06 -->
      <div class="program-card">
        <span class="program-card-num">06</span>
        <h3 class="program-card-title">Urban Hoops</h3>
        <p class="program-card-body">Summer blacktop tournaments and Saturday Night Lights at Curtis High School. Thirty to forty young people on a good night, and a coach who keeps showing up.</p>
        <span class="program-card-meta">Five NYCHA Neighborhoods</span>
      </div>
      <!-- Through-line -->
      <div class="program-card program-card-throughline">
        <h3 class="throughline-heading">The through-line</h3>
        <p class="throughline-body">Thirty-seven of last year's literacy tutors were high-school students from these same neighborhoods, several of them paid through the city's summer jobs program.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ TWO NUMBERS SECTION ══ -->
  <section class="two-numbers-section">
    <span class="two-numbers-label">Two different numbers, kept apart</span>
    <h2 class="two-numbers-heading">We convene a movement much larger than we are. We will not bill you for its size.</h2>
    <p class="two-numbers-intro">Urban Hope anchors a citywide coalition, and its totals are genuinely large. They are not our service numbers. Keeping the two columns separate is the whole point of this page.</p>

    <div class="two-columns">
      <!-- LEFT: Urban Hope numbers -->
      <div class="numbers-col numbers-col-left">
        <span class="col-label col-label-amber">Column One</span>
        <h3 class="col-title col-title-dark">What Urban Hope Inc delivers</h3>
        <p class="col-subtitle col-subtitle-dark">The 501(c)(3) you would be funding.</p>
        <dl class="numbers-table">
          <div class="numbers-row">
            <dt class="numbers-dt numbers-dt-dark">Children in literacy tutoring</dt>
            <dd class="numbers-dd numbers-dd-dark">178</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="numbers-row">
            <dt class="numbers-dt numbers-dt-dark">Children in weekly after-school</dt>
            <dd class="numbers-dd numbers-dd-dark">65</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="numbers-row">
            <dt class="numbers-dt numbers-dt-dark">Teens employed and paid</dt>
            <dd class="numbers-dd numbers-dd-dark">24</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="numbers-row">
            <dt class="numbers-dt numbers-dt-dark">Partner schools</dt>
            <dd class="numbers-dd numbers-dd-dark">8</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="numbers-row">
            <dt class="numbers-dt numbers-dt-dark">Annual revenue, last filed</dt>
            <dd class="numbers-dd numbers-dd-dark">Under $1M</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <span class="col-source col-source-dark">Source: 2025 End-of-Year Report · IRS Form 990</span>
      </div>

      <!-- RIGHT: Coalition numbers -->
      <div class="numbers-col numbers-col-right">
        <span class="col-label col-label-amber">Column Two</span>
        <h3 class="col-title col-title-light">What the coalition we convene delivers</h3>
        <p class="col-subtitle col-subtitle-light">Hundreds of churches. Not our headcount.</p>
        <dl class="numbers-table">
          <div class="numbers-row">
            <dt class="numbers-dt numbers-dt-light">Outreaches coordinated, 2025</dt>
            <dd class="numbers-dd numbers-dd-amber">512</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="numbers-row">
            <dt class="numbers-dt numbers-dt-light">Registered participants</dt>
            <dd class="numbers-dd numbers-dd-amber">3,900</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="numbers-row">
            <dt class="numbers-dt numbers-dt-light">Partner congregations</dt>
            <dd class="numbers-dd numbers-dd-amber">402</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="numbers-row">
            <dt class="numbers-dt numbers-dt-light">Regions, incl. Philadelphia and NJ</dt>
            <dd class="numbers-dd numbers-dd-amber">7</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="numbers-row">
            <dt class="numbers-dt numbers-dt-light">Clergy on the C3 task force</dt>
            <dd class="numbers-dd numbers-dd-amber">8</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <span class="col-source col-source-light">Source: Jesus Week 2025 · C3 Staten Island</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ WHO WE ARE SECTION ══ -->
  <section class="who-section">
    <h2 class="who-heading">A neighborhood organization, not a visiting one.</h2>
    <p class="who-body">Our founder, David Beidel, moved onto the North Shore thirty years ago and stayed. Urban Hope was recognized as a 501(c)(3) in 2011 and is led today by executive director Chad McVann, with a board of nine.</p>
    <p class="who-body">We are a faith-based organization and we say so plainly, because our volunteers and decades of neighborhood trust come from the churches of Staten Island. Read 2 Succeed runs inside DOE buildings and is literacy tutoring only. HopeKidz is an explicitly Christian club that families opt into. We keep that line bright, and we will walk any funder through it.</p>

    <div class="credentials-grid">
      <div class="credential-card">
        <span class="credential-label">Affiliate</span>
        <span class="credential-name">Hope for New York</span>
      </div>
      <div class="credential-card">
        <span class="credential-label">Employer</span>
        <span class="credential-name">NYC SYEP, 3rd year</span>
      </div>
      <div class="credential-card">
        <span class="credential-label">Anchor</span>
        <span class="credential-name">C3 Clergy Task Force</span>
      </div>
      <div class="credential-card">
        <span class="credential-label">Network</span>
        <span class="credential-name">Care Portal</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
